RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE

Office of City Clerk

February 20, 2020

The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne convened in a special meeting on this date
beginning at 6:00 p.m. in Committee Room 104 for the purpose of meeting in Executive Session
involving personnel matters relating to collective labor bargaining with the Cheyenne Professional
Fire Fighters, International Association of Fire Fighters, Local No. 279.  Present were:  MAYOR
- Marian J. Orr; COUNCIL MEMBERS – Mr. Case, Mr. Cook, Mr. Esquibel, Mr. Luna, Dr. Rinne,
Mr. Roybal, Mr. Shanor and Mr. White. Absent:  Mr. Laybourn.  Also present: Kris Jones, City
Clerk; Michael O’Donnell, City Attorney; Alessandra McCoy-Fakelman, Deputy City Attorney;
Robin Lockman, City Treasurer, and Chief Greg Hoggatt, Fire and Rescue Department.  The
pledge of allegiance was not recited due to the absence of a flag.

Mayor Orr advised the meeting would be audio recorded and available on Facebook live
and stated that Wyoming State Statute §16-4-405(a)(x) of the Public Meetings Act allows the
governing body to meet in executive session to consider or tender offers regarding salaries, wages
or other terms and conditions of employment during negotiations with the fire fighters union and
that any motion approved by the governing body to move into executive session during the special
meetings would be pursuant to this section of statute.  Mayor Orr further advised if the governing
body met in executive session, they would be meeting in the Mayor’s Conference Room, and that
Fire Union representatives were welcome to use Committee Room 104 for the purpose of meeting
to caucus.

Spokespersons/representatives for both parties were mutually agreed upon as follows:
Union-TJ Haws and Kevin West and the City-Mayor Orr, Dr. Rinne, City Council President, and
Michael O’Donnell, City Attorney.  It was noted that Dr. Rinne may designate another
Councilmember in the event of his absence.  It was further agreed that both parties would use either
text messaging when returning from executive session or union caucus breaks or utilization of city
administrative staff to notify parties.

Michael O’Donnell, City Attorney, advised the Ground Rules presented are the same as
agreed upon for the FY 2020 contract negotiations with the exception that anyone displaying
disruptive or unruly behaviors will be asked to leave the meeting.  Mr. O’Donnell further advised
the term negotiation is for 2 years.  The City and Union representatives agreed to leave at a 2 year
term, noting this could be modified to a 1 year term.

A recess was requested by Union representatives at 6:12 p.m. for the purpose of reviewing
presented Ground Rules at 6:12 p.m.  The meeting was reconvened at 6:16 p.m.  City and Union
representatives mutually agreed upon the presented ground rules.

The following negotiation terms were agreed upon by both parties:  City will present the
first offer, a 5 minute recess on each hour, allow for 30 minute caucus breaks for Union
```

