representatives and for executive sessions by the governing body which can be expanded upon
mutual agreement, meetings will be scheduled for 2 hours beginning at 6:00 p.m. and ending at
8:00 p.m. unless otherwise agreed upon and meetings will be held in Council Chambers.  Upon
further mutual agreement, the following tentative schedule was announced:  February 25th, 26th,
March 5th, 10, and 12th.   It was noted additional meetings could be scheduled or scheduled
meetings could be cancelled upon mutual agreement.  Mayor Orr confirmed the 30 day negotiation
time frame would expire on 03-14-20.

A recess was called by Union representatives at 6:25 p.m. for the purpose of reviewing the
City’s first contract offer.  The meeting was reconvened at 6:54 p.m.  City and Union
representatives mutually agreed to the following sections as presented:  1, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 10, 11, 14,
16, 27, 29, 30, 31, 32, 33, 36, 38, 39, 40, 42, 43, 44, and 45.

Discussion topics included process for exchanging offer acceptance and rejections between
parties.

Mayor Orr stated the purpose of the special meeting had been met, and there being no
business previously noted for the special meeting, adjourned the meeting at 7:06 p.m.

Submitted by,

Kristina F. Jones,

City Clerk

This notice is available in alternative, accessible formats upon request.

Published:
Wyoming Tribune-Eagle

March 3, 2020
